  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Thomas, \"What do you do with the government's argument that seems to suggest that it's simply an accumulation of the penalties, an aggregation or an increase of the penalties under (c)?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito: \"Can I ask you a -- a question about section (c)(1)(C), capital C --\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, \"And so the government can charge even a death under (c) if it doesn't intend to seek the death penalty?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, \"So, in that situation, is the person convicted under (j) and 1112 or just under (j)?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, \"Well, but why is that, Ms. Ross? I mean, suppose that (j) had not said in the course of a violation of subsection (c) but just repeated all of subsection (c)'s language. Then what?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson: \"I'm asking how the Court looks at -- not -- at (j), not 924(c). What -- why is it absurd for a Congress that is enacting (j) to have had a separate penalty structure that did not incorporate the mandatory minimums of (c) but instead took care of that circumstance through, as the text says here, giving the death penalty, increasing the maximums and the like?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson: \"But that's not the Blockburger test. I don't understand. So you're -- you're suddenly now asking us as a result of this case to revisit Blockburger and what it says about when there are separate offenses?\""
      }
    ],
